{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>וְטֻמְאָתוֹ עָלָיו.</b> The verse speaks of impurity of the body. But a clean person who ate the impure is not punished by karet — only the warning of <b>וְהַבָּשָׂר אֲשֶׁר יִגַּע בְּכָל טָמֵא וגו'</b>. And the warning for an impure person who ate the clean is not stated explicitly in the Torah, but the Sages derived it by a gezerah shavah. Three karets are stated concerning those who eat consecrated foods with impurity of the body, and our Rabbis expounded them in Shevuot: one for the general principle, one for the specific case, and one to teach about the sliding-scale offering — which was stated only for impurity of the Temple and its consecrated things."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:27.687261384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}